.TH ferry-localsend-send 1  Ferry "Ferry Manual"
.SH NAME
ferry\-localsend\-send \- Send files and folders to a LocalSend app. Its name is not verified: anyone on the network can announce any name
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBferry localsend send\fR [\fB\-\-lang\fR] [\fB\-\-pin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-to\fR> <\fIFILES\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send files and folders to a LocalSend app. Its name is not verified: anyone on the network can announce any name
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-lang\fR \fI<CODE>\fR
Interface language for this run (`en`, `pl`); overrides the saved setting
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-to\fR \fI<TO>\fR
Name or IP address (`192.168.1.20` or `192.168.1.20:53317`) of the LocalSend app, as listed by `ferry localsend scan`
.TP
\fB\-\-pin\fR \fI<PIN>\fR
PIN, for apps that require one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFILES\fR>
Files and folders to send (folders keep their structure)
